From 6df4e2a03f9cb0cad0175948d934fa5fc8e53c84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:10:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] quiet-hold: ask quiet-observe-check before taking
 the claim-quiet lease

Follow-up to PR #2606 review 5897651506 nit 1 (card t_01a1d69da65e96cc).

Defect: `hold` ran only the host-file preflight (`start_preflight_reasons`) before
`cq.acquire`. A refusal only the gateway knows (code-attestation route unknowns on any
gateway not on managed-stub / managed-stub-relaunch, coverage pending, drain/restart,
registry unknowns) surfaced only from `quiet-observe-start`, after the lease had committed
the 2 h claim-quiet cooldown.

Fix: after the host-file step and before `cq.acquire`, `hold` asks the read-only bookkeeping
verb `quiet-observe-check` (the same query `--check` uses, shared via `_check_doc`). A
refusal exits 3 (the `--check` code) and prints the same JSON document, with no lease, no
cooldown record and no registry epoch move. A gateway that does not answer (none running,
or an older core without the verb) keeps the earlier behaviour: the hold proceeds and start
stays authoritative (a stderr note says so).

Docs: the module doc and `start_preflight_reasons` no longer say no read-only control verb
exists; they document that `--check` uses start's own 120 s window, while hold's host-file
step subtracts START_PREFLIGHT_MARGIN_S.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_code_attestation_relaunch.py, fixture gateway from
tests/gateway/test_quiet_control.py, served through the production control-socket client):
- near-miss route ledger: hold exits 3, no lease, no last-started.json, observer never
  runs, epoch unchanged. RED at b189612113 ("cooldown was committed").
- relaunch route ledger: hold acquires, the gateway's quiet-observe-start issues an
  observer token, exit 0.
- unsupported verb / no gateway: hold proceeds as before.
